1.3.m:
To the most complete one, worthy of praise, I bow with bliss.
Great Virāj, the receptacle of countless universes, is a fraction of a portion of him;
with bliss I bow to him, the all-pervading lord, the Paramātman, the supreme ruler, // 82

1.4.m:
From their fat, the entire earth was formed completely;
on it indeed exist the worlds, and she is goddess Vasundharā. (29)
Thus ends the fourth chapter, the description of creation, in the Brahmakhaṇḍa of the glorious Brahmavaivarta Mahāpurāṇa, in the dialogue between Sauti and Śaunaka. (4)
